<title>ITALY: IMI, BZW to oversee Turin utility sale.</title>
<headline>IMI, BZW to oversee Turin utility sale.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The city of Turin named Italian bank IMI and Barclays Plc's investment banking arm BZW as global coordinators for the privatisation of the municipal power utility AEM di Torino SpA.</p>
<p>The city aims to sell off 48 percent of the electricity and heating utility's capital, of which 43 percent will go to an industrial partner and five percent to employees and consumers.</p>
<p>The city of Genoa's water and gas utility AMGA was the first municipal utility to be floated and was listed on the Milan bourse in October.</p>
<p>Milan's power utility AEM is also earmarked for privatisation.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 6129589</p>
</text>
